# appearance.painters — PAINTERSCOPE (B482): every kernel file OUTSIDE crates/kernel/src/video/ that puts a colour on
# the glass. appearance-check.py scans video/ plus these files for colour literals (they belong in video/theme.rs).
# This is a PAINTER-FILE list, not an allowlist: a file outside video/ that calls a colour sink (the FrameBuffer
# put/fill/line/scroll methods, the text rasteriser's draw_*, the Pal trait's draw/fill/clear) and is NOT named here
# fails the gate as an `unlisted painter`; a row whose file is gone fails it too.
#   <path under crates/kernel/src>   <what it paints>
console.rs                      the shell console: ground, input ink, selection, scrollback band
ui_status.rs                    the status strip, the pulse instrument panel, the core meters, the LED ramp
splash.rs                       the boot splash: backdrop, beam, spectrum, facet lines, the takeover caption
pal.rs                          the Pal trait's default painters and the shared pointer (fill + shadow)
selftest.rs                     the offscreen pal / glyph vectors
main.rs                         the desktop clears of the boot pumps
arch/aarch64/display_tegra.rs   the Orin format bars, the composite quadrant card, the ladder and rastglass papers
